## Memory Substrate Architecture

This agent uses a two-tier memory model identical to the supervising Hermes agent:

### 1. Local memory — MemPalace (immediate recall)

- MCP endpoint: `{{ openclaw_agent_mempalace_url }}`
- Transport: `{{ openclaw_agent_mempalace_transport }}`
- Purpose: fast, isolated, per-agent retrieval and capture.
- Available tools: MCP server `mempalace` exposes search/retrieve/store hooks.

### 2. Collective memory — Honcho (cross-session, multi-agent)

- Plugin: `{{ openclaw_agent_honcho_plugin }}`
- Base URL: `{{ openclaw_agent_honcho_base_url }}`
- Workspace: `{{ openclaw_agent_honcho_workspace_id }}`
- API key: none (self-hosted)
- Purpose: shared user/peer modeling, conclusions, long-term context across agents.

### 3. Builtin short-term memory

- Backend: `{{ openclaw_agent_memory_backend }}`
- Citation mode: `{{ openclaw_agent_memory_citations }}`

## Model

- Provider: `{{ openclaw_agent_model_provider }}`
- Base URL: `{{ openclaw_agent_model_base_url }}`
- Default model: `{{ openclaw_agent_default_model }}`

## Cattle-not-pet Operations

Reset this instance to a clean state:

```bash
# Stop and remove the container
docker rm -f {{ openclaw_agent_container_name }}

# Wipe data (optional)
sudo rm -rf {{ openclaw_agent_data_dir }} {{ openclaw_agent_log_dir }}

# Re-run the playbook to recreate from immutable image + templates
```

## Useful Commands

```bash
# Container status
docker ps -f name={{ openclaw_agent_container_name }}

# Health check
curl -s http://{{ openclaw_agent_gateway_host }}:{{ openclaw_agent_gateway_port }}/health

# Inspect logs
docker logs -f {{ openclaw_agent_container_name }}

# Run an OpenClaw command inside the container
docker exec -u {{ openclaw_agent_user }} {{ openclaw_agent_container_name }} \
  openclaw --no-color plugins list
```

